        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2019",
        "question_text": "<p>Express $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x - 1)(x + 2)}$ in partial fractions.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Assume $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x - 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{A}{x - 1} + \\frac{B}{x + 2}$.<br>Multiply through by $(x - 1)(x + 2)$: $3x + 5 = A(x + 2) + B(x - 1)$.<br>Solving for $A$ and $B$ gives $A = 2$ and $B = 1$.<br>Thus, the partial fractions are $\\frac{2}{x - 1} + \\frac{1}{x + 2}$.</p>",
